You hit the purple worm.  The purple worm digests you!
The magic-absorbing blade scares the purple worm!
You get regurgitated!
You kill the purple worm!

Normally when you slay an engulfing monster it doesn't leave a corpse, 
AFAIK.

However there seems to be a sequencing issue at work here.  When 
Magicbane scores a special effect the special effect is resolved and 
then the bonus damage is dealt out.

Usually this makes no difference as you simply stun or confuse a monster 
at the same time that you kill it.

But the scare effect causes regurgitation and then the bonus damage for 
rolling a scare is figured, killing a monster that is no longer 
engulfing the hero and so leaving a corpse.

